{"availability":"available","full":"docling-project/docling.rs","name":"docling.rs","description":"Full Rust port of Python docling","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":95,"forks":25,"created":"2026-06-27T16:51:49Z","updated":"2026-10-09T16:59:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://docling-project.github.io/docling.rs/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.410Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.410Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.410Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:39.843Z","stars":93,"forks":23},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:34:45.622Z","stars":93,"forks":23},{"at":"2026-10-06T22:53:26.929Z","stars":94,"forks":23},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:25:25.288Z","stars":94,"forks":24},{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.410Z","stars":95,"forks":25}],"technologies":["Rust"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.410Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Rust port of docling: convert documents into a unified DoclingDocument for downstream AI workflows.","Fast and small: one static binary, no Python/PyTorch at runtime. The PDF ML pipeline runs 4.3× faster than Python docling at 2.3–2.6× less peak RAM (methodology, profiling and per-fixture numbers in docs/PDFCONFORMANCE.md § Performance); declarative formats (DOCX/HTML/XLSX/…) convert 20–60× faster at 60× less memory (measured with scripts/test/performance.sh, Python docling vs Rust on the same file). Output is checked against upstream for every format — see Conformance with Python docling.","▶ Try it in your browser — the whole converter compiled to wasm: drop a DOCX, PDF, XLSX, EPUB … and get Markdown, docling JSON, DocLang XML, LaTeX or a Pandoc AST back. Nothing is uploaded; the page runs entirely on your device, phone included. Scanned pages can be OCR'd there too (layout + PP-OCR + TableFormer via ONNX Runtime Web) once you point it at the models. See crates/docling-wasm."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/docling-project/docling.rs/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"1e3972d8943c6e4abeb7006dad202206310178e2d1ced5e3f777dddbca98c292","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.580Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.580Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T16:59:17Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Rust port of docling: convert documents into a unified DoclingDocument for downstream AI workflows.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/docling-project/docling.rs/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"This server's own option names (strict, password, …) work there too. doctagscontent stays null: there is no DocTags writer (doclangcontent carries its successor). --api-key KEY, or upstream's DOCLINGSERVEAPIKEY, requires X-Api-Key on every /v1 route; /health, /ready, /metrics and the docs page stay open.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/docling-project/docling.rs/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"not_required","text":"The safer default is the operator-pinned mode: set DOCLINGRSVLMENDPOINT / DOCLINGRSVLMMODEL (and optionally APIKEY / PROMPT) on the server and have requests send just pipeline=vlm — callers pick the pipeline, the operator picks where it talks to, and no gate is needed:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/docling-project/docling.rs/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1e3972d8943c6e4abeb7006dad202206310178e2d1ced5e3f777dddbca98c292","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/docling-project/docling.rs/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.585Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/docling-project/docling.rs/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:10.595Z","hash":"1e3972d8943c6e4abeb7006dad202206310178e2d1ced5e3f777dddbca98c292","originalBytes":164939,"storedBytes":164939,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["docling","models","pdf","ocr","page","python","text","json","every","one","default","markdown"